@integrations/skills/sigil/external-guidance-evidence.sigil import { ExternalGuidanceEvidence }

component SigilDesignConversation {
  goal {
    Guide a user from incomplete intent or an existing contract to a coherent,
    modular, and improvable software design through focused material decisions.

    Surface unknowns, conflicts, improvement opportunities, alternatives, and
    pitfalls without replacing user decision authority.
  }

  interface {
    DesignContext {
      supplies the selected component, matching expands, imported and importing
      contracts, relevant boundary summaries, repository evidence, and reviewed
      findings

      distinguishes observed evidence, user-confirmed intent, unresolved ambiguity,
      improvement opportunities, suspected findings, and confirmed problems
    }

    DesignConversation {
      begins only when explicit design, review, or improvement work or a material
      unresolved issue requires user judgment

      operates in exploration, improvement, or correction mode

      presents one primary material decision per turn unless the user requests
      grouped review

      explains why the decision matters, available alternatives, their consequences,
      and a reasoned recommendation

      acknowledges each answer and states its effect on the emerging contract
    }

    DecisionLedger {
      maintains confirmed, provisionally assumed, intentionally deferred, and
      unresolved decisions

      summarizes agreed decisions, remaining blockers, deferrals, improvements, and
      conflicts
    }

    ProposalSynthesis {
      produces exact proposed Sigil only after every blocking decision and confirmed
      material problem is resolved
    }
  }
}

expand SigilDesignConversation {
  state {
    DesignContext {
      Context is sufficient when the affected contract, related ownership and
      dependencies, repository evidence, and material review findings are available
      for the current decision.
    }

    DesignConversation {
      Conversation phase is framing, exploring, resolving, synthesizing, or awaiting
      approval.

      Conversation mode is exploration, improvement, or correction.

      A suspected finding remains under investigation until evidence confirms or
      dismisses it.

      A confirmed material problem keeps the conversation in correction until
      resolved.
    }

    DecisionLedger {
      A material decision is confirmed, provisionally assumed, intentionally
      deferred, or unresolved.
    }

    ProposalSynthesis {
      Synthesis readiness requires no blocking unresolved decision and no unresolved
      confirmed material problem.
    }
  }

  logic {
    DesignContext {
      Consume the component picture produced by semantic and modularity review
      without duplicating graph-discovery mechanics.

      Refresh affected related-Sigil evidence after a material decision and before
      proposal synthesis.
    }

    DesignConversation {
      Enter only for explicit design, review, or improvement work or when a material
      unresolved decision or finding requires user judgment.

      Use exploration mode for incomplete intent, improvement mode for a coherent
      contract with credible improvement opportunities, and correction mode only for
      a confirmed material problem.

      Classify questions by their effect on purpose, boundary, ownership, behavior,
      lifecycle, architecture, risk, and verification.

      Ask the unresolved question whose answer most strongly shapes later decisions.

      Investigate suspected findings proportionally without automatically entering
      correction or blocking unrelated work.

      In correction mode, preserve affected Sigil, explain the exact evidence,
      consequences, risk, alternatives, and recommendation, and ask which intent
      should govern.

      Reopen a confirmed decision when new evidence materially conflicts with it or
      indicates a material improvement opportunity.

      After each answer, restate the resulting decision and identify dependent
      questions, improvements, or conflicts.

      When the user is uncertain, present a conservative recommendation and permit
      only non-blocking uncertainty to be deferred.
    }

    EvidencePacket {
      Request ApplicabilityAssessment from ExternalGuidanceEvidence after sufficient
      framing for each design or review scope.

      Use required or recommended evidence to discover pitfalls, alternatives,
      consequences, uncertainty, and improvement opportunities before presenting
      affected recommendations.

      Treat disagreement between authoritative sources as unresolved design evidence
      when no project decision exists.

      Enter correction mode only when applicable evidence confirms a material
      conflict with approved Sigil or a confirmed user decision.

      Offer a conservative provisional option only when incomplete evidence affects a
      low-risk reversible decision.

      Require missing evidence or qualified review before recommending a definitive
      high-risk or compliance-critical choice.
    }

    DecisionLedger {
      Record each answer with its decision state and effect on unresolved blockers.

      Preserve intentionally deferred decisions in every checkpoint and final
      synthesis.

      Reopen a confirmed decision only when new evidence materially conflicts with it
      or indicates a material improvement opportunity.
    }

    ProposalSynthesis {
      When no blocking decision or confirmed material problem remains, summarize
      confirmed, provisional, deferred, and unresolved decisions before presenting
      exact Sigil.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    DesignConversation {
      Each question materially improves the resulting contract or resolves a material
      finding.

      Existing or approved Sigil is evidence of current intent and is not proof that
      the design cannot be improved.

      A suspected finding does not automatically become a correction or block
      unrelated user work.

      A confirmed material problem cannot be deferred, treated as provisional, or
      bypassed for implementation.

      Independent questions are not presented as an exhaustive questionnaire.

      The user remains the authority for product, architecture, permission, risk, and
      tradeoff decisions.

      Immaterial hypothetical edge cases are not pursued merely for completeness.
    }

    EvidencePacket {
      Evidence informs the conversation without replacing user decision authority.

      Research uncertainty may keep an affected material decision unresolved but does
      not create an independent approval gate.

      A valid packet may be reused without repeated research while its invalidation
      conditions remain unchanged.
    }

    DecisionLedger {
      Provisional assumptions remain visible and do not become confirmed decisions
      implicitly.

      A blocking unresolved decision cannot be intentionally deferred.
    }

    ProposalSynthesis {
      Exact Sigil is not synthesized while a blocking decision or confirmed material
      problem remains unresolved.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    ConversationApplicability {
      Decision: Enter DesignConversation only for explicit design, review, or
      improvement work or when inspected evidence exposes a material decision
      requiring user judgment.

      Scope: Governs invocation of Sigil design conversation; excludes ordinary
      status, explanation, diagnosis, and mechanical work with no material design
      choice.

      Trade-offs: Some requests proceed without a conversational design phase.

      Design issues addressed: Treating design conversation as a mandatory workflow
      stage interrupts unrelated and already-resolved requests.

      Consequences: Conversation is available for proactive improvement without
      activating for every user request.

      Revisit when: The host can deterministically identify material design
      decisions.
    }

    ConversationModes {
      Decision: Use exploration, improvement, and correction as modes of one
      DesignConversation.

      Scope: Governs incomplete designs, review of coherent written contracts, and
      confirmed material problems.

      Trade-offs: The conversation must state its current mode and finding severity
      clearly.

      Design issues addressed: A separate CorrectionConversation duplicates decision
      handling, while treating every suspicion as correction causes premature
      blocking.

      Consequences: Suspected findings are investigated, optional improvements remain
      nonblocking, and only confirmed material problems enter correction mode.

      Revisit when: A materially different authority or communication channel is
      required for correction.
    }

    RelatedDesignContext {
      Decision: Require relevant cross-Sigil and repository context before material
      architectural decisions and recheck affected relationships before synthesis.

      Scope: Governs design and review decisions that can affect component
      boundaries, ownership, interfaces, lifecycle, or dependencies.

      Trade-offs: Material design work incurs focused context-discovery overhead.

      Design issues addressed: Conversation based on an isolated component can
      improve one contract while making related contracts incoherent.

      Consequences: Recommendations account for matching expands, dependencies,
      consumers, boundary summaries, and repository drift.

      Revisit when: Deterministic tooling supplies a complete semantic impact
      analysis.
    }

    EvidenceConsumption {
      Decision: Consume ExternalGuidanceEvidence proactively after framing to
      discover relevant pitfalls, alternatives, and improvements without redefining
      research applicability.

      Scope: Governs evidence use inside DesignConversation.

      Trade-offs: Some design and review work pauses for targeted research.

      Design issues addressed: Requiring prior proof that research will change a
      binding decision suppresses research that would discover valuable improvements.

      Consequences: Existing contracts can receive evidence-informed improvement
      review while irrelevant and repeated research remains avoidable.

      Revisit when: Evidence discovery becomes deterministic or ceases to improve
      design decisions.
    }
  }

  cases {
    DesignConversation {
      A vague product idea enters exploration mode and begins with intended outcome
      and users rather than implementation technology.

      A coherent written contract enters improvement mode when credible evidence
      could materially improve its architecture, modularity, safety, or operation.

      A suspected finding is investigated without automatically entering correction
      or blocking unrelated work.

      A confirmed ownership conflict enters correction mode before proposal synthesis
      or implementation.

      An uncertain user receives a recommendation with consequences rather than an
      unexplained default.
    }

    EvidencePacket {
      A version-sensitive framework choice cites matching official documentation
      while explaining alternatives.

      Conflicting guidance is presented as uncertainty rather than disguised as a
      confident recommendation.

      Missing compliance-critical evidence keeps the affected decision unresolved
      pending qualified review.
    }

    DecisionLedger {
      An intentionally deferred non-blocking decision remains visible in the
      synthesis.
    }

    ProposalSynthesis {
      A permission, destructive-behavior, public-contract ambiguity, or confirmed
      material problem blocks exact Sigil and implementation.
    }
  }
}
